  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Stacked on #651** (#637 step C), which is stacked on #649 and #646. Merge them in order #646, #649, #651, then this. This is **#637 step D**.\n\n**New `CarriedField::column_body(lattice, judged_before) -> Body`** (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/field_body.rs`) reads the carried, clipped field onto the next setup's lattice (`Lattice { x0, y0, cell, nx, ny }`, new frame).\n- **Per column:**\n  - the **top** is one down-march (`march`);\n  - the **floor** is step B's exact shell floor (`floor_at`);\n  - a **flip** swaps them, since the new top is the old floor;\n  - the **clip** trims the column, and `Clip::Empty` leaves every column empty;\n  - a floor a cut reached, or a column the field cannot read, is **refused by name**.\n- **The result** is the same `carry::Body` the column engine makes (new `Body::from_parts`), so `deviate` (the two-sided verdict), `display`, `volume` and `bounds` run **unchanged** on either engine.\n- **Plumbing:** `march::world` is now `pub(crate)`.\n\n**A decision, recorded in `docs/decisions/637-carried-field-read-back.md`:** this replaces the planned `Body = Column | Field` enum. The enum needed a second, field-native implementation of every `Body` method, each new verdict code to prove. The read-back reuses the one verdict the column carry already proves, and tops and floors still come from the field, never interpolated.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/sim/tests/carry_engine_agreement.rs`, 2/2, about 3 s in debug.** The same 20×12 block, cut by the same slot (shallow at z 3, deep at z 1), is carried through **all 8 lattice turns** (quarter turns and flips) on **both** engines.\n  - Per column, `empty_at` matches and the top and floor agree to **1e-6**.\n  - The volumes agree to 1e-6, and `floor_judged` matches.\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** the sim suites pass. Named: field_carry 8, field_floor 3, stock_backend_parity 13, stock_columns 3, and app setup_carry 9, carried_verify 8, rest_across_setups 7.\n- **Clippy** on sim and app with `-D warnings`: clean. No golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **Step E:** the app holders (#586) taking a field carry. Nothing in the app calls `column_body` yet.\n- **A field-native verdict finer than the lattice:** possible later behind the same `Body` API.\n- **The two #651 nits** (a `Display` for `ClipRefusal`, and the mod sort order) are left for step E, which touches the same file.\n\nChangelog: none (internal: the carried field reads back as a column body; not yet used)\n\nRefs #637\nRefs #26\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
